{"id": "tea:atmasiddhi:1", "source": "src:atmasiddhi", "location": {"ref": "1", "section": null}, "paraphrase": "Not understanding my own nature I suffered endlessly; I bow to the holy true teacher who made that state understood.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "devotional", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion", "knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["teacher-transmission"], "terms": ["trm:sadguru"], "concepts": ["cpt:sadguru-marks"], "teachers": ["tch:srimad-rajacandra"], "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U35-jain-philosophy"], "disagreements": []}, "correction_log": [], "recent": true, "notes": "Verse number recalled, not checked; the content is the unit author's recollection (skeleton).", "coverage": ["B2"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U35-jain-philosophy"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:atmasiddhi:10", "source": "src:atmasiddhi", "location": {"ref": "10", "section": null}, "paraphrase": "The marks of the true teacher: knowledge of the self, equal vision, acting only as past karma unfolds, unprecedented speech, and supreme scriptural knowledge.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge", "devotion"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["teacher-transmission"], "terms": ["trm:sadguru"], "concepts": ["cpt:sadguru-marks"], "teachers": ["tch:srimad-rajacandra"], "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U35-jain-philosophy"], "disagreements": []}, "correction_log": [], "recent": true, "notes": "Verse number recalled, not checked; the content is the unit author's recollection (skeleton).", "coverage": ["B2"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U35-jain-philosophy"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:atmasiddhi:142", "source": "src:atmasiddhi", "location": {"ref": "142", "section": null}, "paraphrase": "Countless salutations at the feet of the knower whose state, though in a body, is beyond the body.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "devotional", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion", "knowledge"], "stage": "realized"}, "types": ["ultimate", "karma-liberation"], "terms": ["trm:sadguru"], "concepts": ["cpt:siddha-state"], "teachers": ["tch:srimad-rajacandra"], "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U35-jain-philosophy"], "disagreements": []}, "correction_log": [], "recent": true, "notes": "Closing dohā; living liberation in the body (the kevalin/sadguru). Verse number recalled, not checked; the content is the unit author's recollection (skeleton).", "coverage": ["B2"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U35-jain-philosophy"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:atmasiddhi:24-33", "source": "src:atmasiddhi", "location": {"ref": "24-33", "section": null}, "paraphrase": "The one attached to opinions (matārthī) takes the outward monk or family tradition for the teacher, clings to rites or to dry talk of the self, and does not seek the true teacher.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "polemical", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["teacher-transmission", "dispute"], "terms": ["trm:matarthi"], "obstacles": ["obs:ekanta-view"], "teachers": ["tch:srimad-rajacandra"], "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U35-jain-philosophy"], "disagreements": []}, "correction_log": [], "recent": true, "notes": "Range recalled.", "coverage": ["B2"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "low", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U35-jain-philosophy"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:atmasiddhi:34-42", "source": "src:atmasiddhi", "location": {"ref": "34-42", "section": null}, "paraphrase": "The self-seeker (ātmārthī) seeks the true teacher, has calm of passions, longing for liberation, weariness with worldly life and compassion, and so becomes fit for self-realisation.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge", "devotion"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["teacher-transmission", "practice"], "terms": ["trm:atmarthi"], "concepts": ["cpt:sadguru-marks"], "teachers": ["tch:srimad-rajacandra"], "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U35-jain-philosophy"], "disagreements": []}, "correction_log": [], "recent": true, "notes": "Range recalled.", "coverage": ["B2"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "low", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U35-jain-philosophy"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:atmasiddhi:43", "source": "src:atmasiddhi", "location": {"ref": "43", "section": null}, "paraphrase": "The soul exists, it is eternal, it is the doer of its karma, it is the enjoyer, liberation exists, and the means of liberation is the true dharma.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["ultimate", "karma-liberation"], "terms": ["trm:satpada"], "concepts": ["cpt:six-fundamentals"], "teachers": ["tch:srimad-rajacandra"], "disputes": ["dsp:is-there-a-self"], "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U35-jain-philosophy"], "disagreements": []}, "correction_log": [], "recent": true, "notes": "Verse number recalled, not checked; the content is the unit author's recollection (skeleton).", "coverage": ["B2"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U35-jain-philosophy"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
